s we try, the better. These rarities may be new mutations, or they can be existing ones that are neutral—or are even selected against—in a wild population. A good example is mutations that disrupt seed dispersal, leaving the seeds on the heads long after they are ripe.", "reference": "2013 May-June, David Van Tassel, Lee DeHaan, “Wild Plants to the Rescue”, in American Scientist, volume 101, number 3:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "بَعْدَمَا"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "след като"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "després que"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "acabat que"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "en acabat que"}, {"language": {"code": "zdj", "name": "Ngazidja Comorian"}, "word": "ɓaȃɗa"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "nadat"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "kun"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "sen jälkeen, kun"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "après que"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "nachdem"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "αφού"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "αφότου"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "miután"}, {"language": {"code": "it", "name": "Italian"}, "word": "dopo"}, {"language": {"code": "lo", "name": "Lao"}, "word": "ຫລັງຈາກ"}, {"language": {"code": "la", "name": "Latin"}, "word": "postquam"}, {"language": {"code": "ml", "name": "Malayalam"}, "word": "ശേഷം"}, {"language": {"code": "nb", "name": "Norwegian Bokmål"}, "word": "etter"}, {"language": {"code": "nb", "name": "Norwegian Bokmål"}, "word": "etter at"}, {"language": {"code": "no", "name": "Norwegian Nynorsk"}, "word": "etter"}, {"language": {"code": "no", "name": "Norwegian Nynorsk"}, "word": "etter at"}